  "theorem_name": "PointwiseLogLogDefectStrictStrengthCalibration",
  "declared_proposition": "At every Chen-positive even N, with C(N)=R(N)+S(N) and L(N)=S(N)-R(N), the exact identity delta(N)=1-L(N)/C(N)=2R(N)/C(N) implies R(N)>0 if and only if delta(N)>0. Thus any lower bound delta(N)>=c/log log N for every sufficiently large even N already implies strong Goldbach and is quantitatively stronger than positivity. Channel algebra and Goldbach positivity alone cannot imply it: the integer model N=2^m, C=N/m, R=1, S=C-1 for powers of two m has R>0 while delta log log N tends to zero.",
  "mathematical_argument": "The projector identity C-L=2R gives the equivalence because C is positive. In the abstract model delta=2/C=2m/2^m. For m>=2, log log(2^m)=log(m log 2)<=m, so delta log log N<=2m^2/2^m, which tends to zero. Hence no fixed c>0 follows from one representation per target, even when the ambient channel has the natural N/log N scale.",
